! mcp_bootstrap_p360.strap -- MCP printed page 360: the $DUMP program's
! character tables -- the hex-digit table AHXTB, the instruction
! mnemonic tables (ATRNTB .. AIMNTB), the indicator-name table
! AINDCR, the floating-point mnemonic tables AFLTBL/AOPTBL, the
! T/U/V flag table AFLGTB, and the words AFXW1 and ADMPBG; lines 1-55.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_250-445.pdf PDF p.110, read at 400 dpi, doubtful
! glyphs at 900 dpi.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 22$DUMP
!  CARD ID VB000832  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 360"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 236231, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  55 lines; every line number prints a "*".  "*" after the
! LOCATION on lines 18, 23, 26, 29, 32, 35, 39, 41, 45, 49, 53.  Lines
! 25, 28, 37 are CNOPs that print no location and no binary (the
! counter is already on a full word); lines 22, 42, 48 are CNOPs that
! print 000000.30 00.  No remarks.  No TAIL.  Located rows contiguous
! from 236231.50 (line 1) to 236425.00 (line 55, VF; next 236425.31).
!
! (A*)DD / (A()DD CHARACTER DATA.  Thirty-one rows are entry-mode A
! character strings at eight bits a character (the location column
! confirms: MASK, four characters, 236231.50 -> 236232.10).  They print
! no binary, so no !CHECK; their LENGTHS are checked by the next
! labelled row's !SYM.  Every blank run was counted on a fixed 39.8 px
! (400 dpi) character grid laid on the statement column (per-glyph
! centres within 0.2 of a cell) and agrees with the printed location
! sequence: every row's length equals the next location's distance,
! or, before a CNOP, rounds up to the CNOP's printed half word (lines
! 21: 21 characters -> 236253.20, CNOP at .40; 41: 35 -> 236361.30,
! CNOP at .40; 47: 35 -> 236405.30, CNOP at .40).  The WHOLE sequence
! was also assembler-checked: a scratch copy with the six "(A()" rows
! (below) rewritten "(A*)...*" and the stand-ins removed -- the same
! bits, since the datum is cut at its LAST terminator -- passes every
! !SYM and the CNOP checks at 236361.40 and 236405.40.  The copy was
! discarded; this deck keeps the printed form.  Corroboration: each
! AFLTBL/AOPTBL row ends with a flag digit that joins the next row's
! first entry (1|+MG, 1|D+, 1|D+MG, 3|ST, 7|LWF, 9|KF), which holds
! only if every count is exact.  Six rows (38-41, 45,
! 47) print the entry mode "(A()": the end-of-statement character is
! "(" because their data contain "*" (C28-6129 printed p.16, the
! programmer's choice of terminator), and each ends with "(".
!
! JOIN.  p.359 (PDF p.109) ends with line 56, ATR16 (A*)DD(BU),TR-16*
! at 236231.00, five characters: next 236231.50 = line 1.  p.361 (PDF
! p.111) opens line 2 at 236425.31 (PUNFUL, (CC*)DD, card series
! WA000001, still PUNID 22$DUMP): contiguous with line 55's VF (25
! bits).
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * line 29, statement column 30 (data column 20, the 4th character
!     of the "TS" cell, between "TS" and "CPUSEKJ"): a small low wedge,
!     14x22 px at 400 dpi, at the baseline in its own cell.  Set beside
!     this row's LOCATION period at 900 dpi it is NOT that glyph (the
!     period is a solid round dot, 27x29 px, standing higher) nor the
!     comma (16x33, tailed).  Written BLANK ("TS  ", as every other
!     4-character indicator cell).  A one-byte judgment nothing checks
!     (the row prints no binary; the length is 48 either way) --
!     REPORTED.  If it is a partial strike, the byte is "." not blank.
!   * line 40 "-CL": the C has the straight left side of this drum's
!     worn D (cf. line 30 "DS" vs "CS"); line 41 prints "-DLWF" plainly:
!     written "-DL".  Line 47 "TDCV" kept as read (D with stem).
!   * line 30 "EOP", "OP"; line 35 "MOP"; line 40 "1SLO": the open
!     rounded-rectangle glyph is this drum's O (C prints round): O.
!   * line 53 "UVT", "TUV": the U's (columns 21, 33) print with a worn
!     right stem, like L; the row is an eight-entry 3-character table
!     of the T/U/V flag combinations ("   ","  V"," U "," UV","T  ",
!     "T V","TU ","TUV"), so U.
!   * lines 54, 55 "XW,C,9" and "VF,C": open round = digit 0; both
!     assemble to the printed zero value fields.
!   * labels: line 23 prints "ACRNCX" (both D's worn; = ADRNDX, as
!     scratch p.355 spells it), line 29 "AINCCR" read AINDCR (4th glyph
!     the worn D, 5th a round C; scratch p.355 AINDCR), line 43
!     "ACPTBL" = AOPTBL (open O; scratch p.352 AOPTBL), line 55 ADMPBG
!     (D worn; landed pp.342-343 ADMPBG).
!   * line 34 "PG0": digit 0, with its numbered family PG1-PG6.
!   * line 20 "BZB1BB1", lines 38-47 leading "1": digit 1 (flagged, no
!     top serif), not I.
!
! ENTRY MODE "(A()".  Lines 38, 39, 40, 41, 45, 47 print "(A()DD(BU),...":
! the end-of-statement character is "(" because their data hold "*".
! C28-6129 printed p.29: "(Az)DD ... alphabetic information to "z"" --
! z is any one character.  Until 2026-11-06 strap_asm's prefix scan
! counted parentheses and refused these cards.
!
! EXTERNALS.  None: the page references no symbol it does not define.
!
! CARD SERIALS.  VB000832 .. VB000871.  Lines 2-17 share VB000833 (one
! (8)DD card compiling sixteen bytes); every other line has its own
! serial.  None skipped.

        SLC, (8)236231.50
AMASK   (A*)DD(BU),MASK* ! line  1
AHXTB   (8)DD(BU,8),12,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,10,11,61,62,63,64,65,66 ! line  2  (rows lines 2-17)
ATRNTB  (A*)DD(BU),T     SWAP  TI    SWAPI TB    SWAPB TBI   SWAPBI* ! line 18
AMISTB  (A*)DD(BU),R   RCZ EX  EXICZ   * ! line 19
ABRBTB  (A*)DD(BU),BZB BB  BZBZBBZ BZBNBBN BZB1BB1 * ! line 20
ABRTBL  (A*)DD(BU),BE BD B  BR BEW   NOP* ! line 21
        CNOP ! line 22
ADRNDX  (A*)DD(BU),LX  LV  LC  LR  KV  V+  V+C V+CRSX  SV  SC  * ! line 23
        (A*)DD(BU),SR  KC  LVE SVA RNX * ! line 24
        CNOP ! line 25
ANXBR   (A*)DD(BU),CB   CBZ  CBR  CBRZ CBH  CBZH CBRH CBRZHCB+  * ! line 26
        (A*)DD(BU),CBZ+ CBR+ CBRZ+CB-  CBZ- CBR- CBRZ-* ! line 27
        CNOP ! line 28
AINDCR  (A*)DD(BU),MK  IK  IJ  EK  TS  CPUSEKJ UNRJCBJ EPGKUK  EE  * ! line 29  (stray mark in data col 20: written blank, see header)
        (A*)DD(BU),EOP CS      OP  AD  USA EXE DS  DF  IF  LC  PF  * ! line 30
        (A*)DD(BU),ZD  * ! line 31
        (A*)DD(BU),IR  LS  PSH XPFPXPO XPH XPL XPU ZM  RU  TF  UF  * ! line 32
        (A*)DD(BU),VF  * ! line 33
        (A*)DD(BU),XF  BTR DTR PG0 PG1 PG2 PG3 PG4 PG5 PG6 XCZ * ! line 34
        (A*)DD(BU),XVLZXVZ XVGZXL  XE  XH  MOP RLZ RZ  RGZ RN  * ! line 35
        (A*)DD(BU),AL  AE  AH  NM  * ! line 36
        CNOP ! line 37
AFLTBL  (A()DD(BU),+   -L   1M+  -ST  1K   1KR  1*   1/   1( ! line 38
        (A()DD(BU),+MG -LWF 1M+MG-SRD 1KMG 1KMGR1*+  9R/  1( ! line 39
        (A()DD(BU),D+  -DL  1LFT 1SLO 1F+  -E+  -D*  1D/  1( ! line 40  (printed "-CL", D worn)
        (A()DD(BU),D+MG-DLWF1     SRT 5SHF 1E+I 2STM 1( ! line 41
        CNOP ! line 42
AOPTBL  (A*)DD(BU),+   1LCV 7L   3     M+  -LFT 3* ! line 43
        (A*)DD(BU),ST  2C   9K   3KE  3KR  3     * ! line 44
        (A()DD(BU),*   3CV  6/   3CM  9+MG 1LTRC7( ! line 45
        (A*)DD(BU),LWF 3     M+MG-M+1 -SRD 2CT  9* ! line 46
        (A()DD(BU),KF  3KFE 3KFR 3     *+  TDCV 6LTRS3( ! line 47
        CNOP ! line 48
AIMNTB  (A*)DD(BU),C+I  LVI  LCI  LRI  KVI  V+I  V+IC V+ICRC-I  LVNI * ! line 49
        (A*)DD(BU),KCI  LVS  KVNI V-I  V-IC V-ICR* ! line 50
ASIC    (A*)DD(BU),SIC* ! line 51
AERROR  (A*)DD(BU),ERROR* ! line 52
AFLGTB  (A*)DD(BU),     V U  UVT  T VTU TUV* ! line 53  (U at cols 21, 33 prints worn)
AFXW1   XW,0,9 ! line 54  (printed "XW,C,9": open 0; the label ends in a flagged 1, as p.357 line 2 prints it)
ADMPBG  VF,0 ! line 55  (printed "VF,C": open 0)

!SYM AMASK 236231.50
!SYM AHXTB 236232.10
!SYM ATRNTB 236234.10
!SYM AMISTB 236242.10
!SYM ABRBTB 236244.50
!SYM ABRTBL 236250.50
!SYM ADRNDX 236254.00
!SYM ANXBR 236264.00
!SYM AINDCR 236276.00
!SYM AFLTBL 236336.00
!SYM AOPTBL 236362.00
!SYM AIMNTB 236406.00
!SYM ASIC 236420.00
!SYM AERROR 236420.30
!SYM AFLGTB 236421.00
!SYM AFXW1 236424.00
!SYM ADMPBG 236425.00
!CHECK 236232.10 | 012 | line 2 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 012 | 8
!CHECK 236232.20 | 001 | line 3 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 001 | 8
!CHECK 236232.30 | 002 | line 4 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 002 | 8
!CHECK 236232.40 | 003 | line 5 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 003 | 8
!CHECK 236232.50 | 004 | line 6 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 004 | 8
!CHECK 236232.60 | 005 | line 7 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 005 | 8
!CHECK 236232.70 | 006 | line 8 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 006 | 8
!CHECK 236233.00 | 007 | line 9 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 007 | 8
!CHECK 236233.10 | 010 | line 10 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 010 | 8
!CHECK 236233.20 | 011 | line 11 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 011 | 8
!CHECK 236233.30 | 061 | line 12 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 061 | 8
!CHECK 236233.40 | 062 | line 13 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 062 | 8
!CHECK 236233.50 | 063 | line 14 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 063 | 8
!CHECK 236233.60 | 064 | line 15 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 064 | 8
!CHECK 236233.70 | 065 | line 16 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 065 | 8
!CHECK 236234.00 | 066 | line 17 AHXTB (8)DD(BU,8) value 066 | 8
!CHECK 236253.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 22 CNOP
!CHECK 236361.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 42 CNOP
!CHECK 236405.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 48 CNOP
!CHECK 236424.00 | 000000.00+ 000 000011 000000 | line 54 AFXW1 XW,0,9 (printed "XW,C,9", open 0)
!CHECK 236425.00 | 000000.00+ | line 55 ADMPBG VF,0 (printed "VF,C", open 0)
